<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/Phillips-Farm4.jpg" alt="A painting of trees with an abstract impressionistic foreground against a yellow sky" width="550" height="451" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Phillips Farm IV. 20x24, oil on linen. 2014</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I painted this landscape as my entry for this year's Waterford Fair art show. &nbsp;I worked on some of the ideas behind this painting over the course of the summer, particularly the effect of light through the trees.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The foreground is a mixture of brush and palette knife painting over a transparent block in. &nbsp;I painted the darks in the tree line with an opaque mixture of burnt umber, viridian and alizarin crimson, cooled with a bit of white because I won't have time to varnish the painting before the show and it will otherwise look too flat.</p>